    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n**Before:** `sp-dashboard-public-conditions` was empty, the privacy mode only changed on `P`/`g`, and TODO lines were not clickable by default.\n\n**After:**\n- `sp-dashboard-condition-focus` is the default condition. True while `sp-dashboard-focus-flag-file` exists (a macOS Shortcuts automation can `touch`/`rm` it when a Focus turns on/off), or while macOS lists a Focus as on in `~/Library/DoNotDisturb/DB/Assertions.json`. `sp-dashboard-focus-modes` limits it to some Focus modes.\n- `M-x sp-dashboard-public-facing-mode`: global minor mode, lighter ` Public`, forces public mode (private entries hidden) over the other settings.\n- The dashboard remembers whether it was drawn as public. A timer (`sp-dashboard-public-check-interval`, 30 s) and file watches on the two Focus files compare that to the current status while the buffer exists, and toggling the mode does so too. A visible Dashboard is redrawn in its window; a hidden one is killed, so it never comes back showing entries it should now hide.\n- `sp-dashboard-agenda-todos-clickable` is now `t`: `RET` or a click on a TODO visits the entry (each TODO is a `TAB` stop).\n- Doc and CHANGELOG updated; the doc tangles to the `.el`.\n\n**Checked** (Emacs 29.3, headless): flag file on/off redraws and hides/shows the private entry; the minor mode forces and releases public; the Assertions parser and the mode filter work on a made-up file; clicking a TODO opens its Org file at the entry. **Not checked:** macOS itself. The real `Assertions.json` layout and whether Emacs can read it (it may need Full Disk Access) are from memory, so the flag-file route is the reliable one.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01T2BcMQ3qdNUiW5oZRLQRsG)_",
